{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/729452-a-question-concerning-malfeans","id":729452,"title":"A Question concerning Malfeans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T11:24:36-07:00","id":729452,"title":"A Question concerning Malfeans","content":"So, another day, another slightly awkward meta-question to be asked. Malfeans. To be clear, I'm talking about the kind of near God's of Oblivion that were hinted at in Wraith and confirmed in Orpheus.<br /> <br /> I'm here looking for some creativity as to how a group of players might go about tackling one. I'm aware, that these things are more plot device than they are true characters or enemies. But in a 'Stop the Malfean or the end is -certain-'. How would player characters go about it? If one ever got out of the Labyrinth, using a number of Oblivion tainted Wraiths as conduits to get through, and rose in Scotland, beginning a slow and destructive descent into the UK, how could it be stopped?<br /> <br /> In this instance, the players in question could range from any cWoD race, except Kuei-Jin and Mage. <br /> <br /> I'm open to as much out of the box thinking as possible, on this. I'm just curious to see what others make of the problem faced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T13:22:21-07:00","id":729753,"title":"","content":"Well, if one excludes those two splats very few non-Wraith characters would ever be aware of big goings-on in the Underworld. Maybe the Dunsirn branch of the Giovanni would be concerned, or members of the Orphic Circle? I'm guessing that fairly extensive ghostly armies with use of relic artillery and planes would need to be involved to take down a Malfean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T14:43:42-07:00","id":729941,"title":"","content":"I think if one spilled out of the Labyrinth into the world... the other supernaturals would notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T20:31:16-07:00","id":730937,"title":"","content":"Malfeans themselves are not much active. It's their spectral cults going about their work based on what they imagine their Malfeans masters want them to do. Concentrate on stopping the cultists' plans - you can use any number of Call of Cthulhu adventures as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T01:59:53-07:00","id":731753,"title":"","content":"I'm also thinking that trying to lure them back into the Labyrinth and put them back into their famed slumbers might be an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:59:36-07:00","id":732866,"title":"","content":"I had something like a Once-born appear in the backstory of my game. Three septs of Garou came together to fight the Ravenous Ghost when it started trying to push through the Gauntlet, and nearly all of them died... and they didn't even destroy the thing, it just sank back into the dark umbra and went back to sleep.<br /> <br /> As Black Fox said, combating them indirectly by fighting their minions and cults is the way to go.<br /> Malfeans are not meant to be direct opponents, unless you want to kill your player characters. If you water-down the threat posed by the God-Kings of Oblivion, it cheapens the threat that they pose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:59:22-07:00","id":733140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/729452-a-question-concerning-malfeans?p=732866#post732866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had something like a Once-born appear in the backstory of my game. Three septs of Garou came together to fight the Ravenous Ghost when it started trying to push through the Gauntlet, and nearly all of them died... and they didn't even destroy the thing, it just sank back into the dark umbra and went back to sleep.<br /> <br /> As Black Fox said, combating them indirectly by fighting their minions and cults is the way to go.<br /> Malfeans are not meant to be direct opponents, unless you want to kill your player characters. If you water-down the threat posed by the God-Kings of Oblivion, it cheapens the threat that they pose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:46:17-07:00","id":734435,"title":"","content":"Yeah, fighting Malfeans should be akin to fighting gods. You'd probably be fighting smaller battles in a greater war, going up against the minions of the gods rather than the gods directly. At best, you'd hope for minor triumphs, but over an epic chronicle you might get to make some significant victories. Short of becoming gods themselves, however, there's little chance of PCs standing directly against Malfeans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}